# implements-port slice 11 (B2; Q43; REVIEW 914ae15, fable_pc's M43/P43): unit_s7_prim_cross over its own convert.lm2
# whose size_t -> int row has the receiver lm_stg_convert_size_t_int + 0 (tests/unit_s7_conv_cellneed_expr_table.lm2) -- one
# argument that is no name: said at the cell, "a conversion table cell this row needs is not a name (evaluating a
# table argument is not ported yet)".  A name only for a cell that is one atom holds for expressions too, not only
# for Structures (M43 -- the check dropped -- took the first atom and accepted).
fn: go () int
    int: a 1
    size_t: b 2U
    a: b
    return: a

int: k
k: go()
if: k = 2
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 1; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
